{"type": "text", "timestamp": 1793758773736, "sessionID": "ses_e5ba5ad0affe2a78jyFGIIJ4sI", "part": {"id": "prt_1a45ab49c001yYfMCwGya21I4c", "messageID": "msg_1a45aa1b1001g41qNTjUBXn2PV", "sessionID": "ses_e5ba5ad0affe2a78jyFGIIJ4sI", "type": "text", "text": "**BillingService and PaymentsService would lose notification-message delivery**: both call **NotificationsAPI**, whose delivery backend is **NotificationsService**, which stores data in **NotificationsRedisInstance**.\n\nThe graph also identifies two indirectly affected services:\n- **RenewalsWorker** \u2014 depends on **BillingService**.\n- **ReportingService** \u2014 depends on **BillingService**.\n\n**Evidence limitation:** The tools confirm the two callers of `NotificationsAPI` and the `NotificationsService \u2192 NotificationsRedisInstance` storage relationship, but do not expose a link between `NotificationsAPI` and `NotificationsService`. Thus, the delivery impact above assumes that API is backed by that service. The indirect dependencies alone do not establish that RenewalsWorker or ReportingService sends messages.", "time": {"start": 1793758770332, "end": 1793758773734}, "metadata": {"openai": {"itemId": "msg_05363b24f15a987e016aea9632443487d08628a39a7ee28585", "phase": "final_answer"}}}}
